{
  "id": "EDU033",
  "title": "The Example Loses Its Training Wheels",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "learning/study",
  "premise": "A learner wants to solve a new worked problem, but copying every displayed step hides which choices are understood. Successively removing selected steps invites the learner to supply and check them.",
  "hook": "This time, one step is missing. What belongs here?",
  "visible_action": "A completed solution scroll replaces first one, then several blocks with empty sockets that accept learner choices.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Worked examples can become practice when support is deliberately reduced.",
  "gate": "Review scaffolding claims; keep example difficulty and prerequisite knowledge explicit.",
